        "char_end": 964,
        "char_start": 882,
        "episode_id": "ep-febd9a8f53bf3a3a",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-01",
        "text": "I want to dig into that. What's the version of the question that actually matters?",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 42000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 36000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p04_e01.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "quote:296266b8334d4fe3",
      "properties": {
        "char_end": 1142,
        "char_start": 978,
        "episode_id": "ep-febd9a8f53bf3a3a",
        "speaker_id": "person:speaker-02",
        "text": "It comes down to this: Strobe positioning at 45 degrees is the starting point, not the destination. Once you internalize that, the rest of the decisions get easier.",
        "timestamp_end_ms": 48000,
        "timestamp_start_ms": 42000,
        "transcript_ref": "transcripts/p04_e01.txt"
      },
      "type": "Quote"
    },
